From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <luke@agent54.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/50] controlledframe/guest view: keep guest across moveBefore() (connectedMoveCallback)

Moving a <webview>, <controlledframe> or <extensionoptions> element, or one
of its ancestors, with Node.moveBefore() disconnects and reconnects it
without destroying it. The guest view container element used to treat the
reconnect like a new attach and created a second guest. Handle
connectedMoveCallback so that the element stays bound to its existing guest;
removing the element still destroys the guest.

Tests: WebViewTest.Shim_TestMoveBeforeKeepsGuest,
ControlledFrameMoveBeforeTest.MoveBeforeKeepsGuest and a matching
ExtensionWebUIEmbeddedOptionsTest case.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/apps/guest_view/web_view_browsertest.cc b/chrome/browser/apps/guest_view/web_view_browsertest.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/apps/guest_view/web_view_browsertest.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/apps/guest_view/web_view_browsertest.cc
@@ -2461,6 +2461,22 @@
   GetGuestViewManager()->WaitForLastGuestDeleted();
 }
 
+// Moving a <webview>, or one of its ancestors, with Node.moveBefore() must keep
+// the element bound to its existing guest. It must not create a second guest,
+// and removing the element must still destroy the guest.
+IN_PROC_BROWSER_TEST_P(WebViewTest, Shim_TestMoveBeforeKeepsGuest) {
+  ASSERT_NO_FATAL_FAILURE(
+      TestHelper("testMoveBeforeKeepsGuest", "web_view/shim", NO_TEST_SERVER));
+  ASSERT_EQ(1u, GetGuestViewManager()->num_guests_created());
+  ASSERT_EQ(1u, GetGuestViewManager()->GetCurrentGuestCount());
+
+  // Exactly one guest exists here, so waiting for all guests waits for it.
+  ASSERT_TRUE(content::ExecJs(GetFirstAppWindowWebContents(),
+                              "document.querySelector('webview').remove();"));
+  GetGuestViewManager()->WaitForAllGuestsDeleted();
+  EXPECT_EQ(0u, GetGuestViewManager()->GetCurrentGuestCount());
+}
+
 // Remove <webview> immediately after navigating it.
 // This is a regression test for http://crbug.com/40077958.
